<!--
    =============================================================================
    URL Navigator — Flow URL Redirect (canonical package manifest)
    =============================================================================

    Registered namespace (2GP): cvplus — product / listing name: URL Navigator.

    This manifest is the single source of truth for what ships in this slice:
    one Lightning web component bundle only.

    LightningComponentBundle: flowUrlRedirect
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    • Target: lightning__FlowScreen (Flow Screen element).
    • Purpose: Navigate the user to a Flow-supplied URL (same tab or new tab),
      with client-side validation (http/https only, optional org-relative path,
      no credentials in URL, length and obfuscation checks). See the bundle’s
      urlRedirectUtils.js for the exact rules.
    • Inputs (Flow): Public URL / targetUrl (String, required), openInNewWindow (Boolean).

    Repo documentation (not deployed as metadata)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    • docs/PACKAGE_DOCUMENTATION.md — Package documentation and reviewer appendix
    • docs/SECURITY_REVIEW_SUBMISSION_STEPS.md — Partner Security Review submission checklist
    • docs/SECURITY_REVIEW_QUESTIONNAIRE.md — Draft questionnaire answers for Partner portal
    • docs/README-url-navigator-PACKAGE.md — namespace, CLI, 2GP pointers

    • 2GP: package alias cvplus (see sfdx-project.json → packageAliases).

    Deploy (Salesforce CLI)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    npm script: deploy:urlNavigator (see package.json).

    =============================================================================
-->
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <types>
        <members>flowUrlRedirect</members>
        <name>LightningComponentBundle</name>
    </types>
    <version>66.0</version>
</Package>
